  "exhibits": [
    {
      "id": "isc-m1-tbs2-ex1",
      "title": "Process flow",
      "html": "<p>The ERP matches invoices with orders and receipts. Vendor bank-account changes can be made and approved by the same user. A robot exports payment totals but drops rejected records from its report.</p>"
    },
    {
      "id": "isc-m1-tbs2-ex2",
      "title": "Control objective",
      "html": "<p>Payments should be authorized, directed to valid recipients, completely recorded, and reconciled. The matching rule alone does not address every objective.</p>"
    }
  ],
  "explanation": "<h3>Classification of the three-way match</h3><p>The match controls a specific transaction-processing function.</p><h3>Vendor-change weakness</h3><p>Self-approved master-data changes can redirect payments.</p><h3>Risk from omitted rejected records</h3><p>Rejected records may need investigation and reconciliation.</p><h3>Best next step</h3><p>End-to-end understanding connects each risk to an appropriate control.</p>"
